PART B — MULTI-DEVICE SYNC SYSTEM

3. Core Multi-Device Sync Philosophy

Implement Multi-Device Sync as a completely optional system using:

- Google Sign-In through Android Credential Manager.
- Firebase Authentication.
- Cloud Firestore.
- The existing "MultiDeviceSyncCoordinator" architecture, if already implemented.

The application must follow an Offline-First Architecture.

Users must be able to use all local RESOLVE features without creating an account or connecting Google.

Signing in should enable selected cloud features without making Firebase a dependency for the core focus-lock functionality.

The local application must remain fully usable when:

- The user stays signed out.
- Internet connectivity is unavailable.
- Firebase is temporarily unavailable.
- Cloud synchronization is paused.
- The user signs out.

Cloud synchronization must never become a prerequisite for starting, maintaining, or completing a local lock session.

4. Account Connection Flow

