FINAL DEVELOPMENT PRINCIPLE

RESOLVE must behave as one integrated application, not as a collection of disconnected features.

The local lock engine must remain reliable even when Firebase, internet connectivity, or animations are unavailable.

Cloud synchronization must be optional, secure, and predictable.

Every device must maintain its own local security configuration while participating in explicitly authorized cross-device lock synchronization.

Every screen must adapt smoothly to the available device dimensions.

Every animation must improve the visual experience without affecting functionality.

Preserve existing working implementations, avoid unnecessary rewrites, and prioritize correctness, stability, privacy, performance, and a consistent premium user experience.

Implement the complete plan within the existing RESOLVE project, verify each stage, and do not claim completion until the relevant functionality has actually been implemented and tested.